                <pb facs="0409" n="289" xml:id="pg289"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Chargé
                    Sleeper.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-09-21"><hi rendition="#italic">September 21,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Adee informs Mr. Sleeper that the Cuban minister expressed his regrets at
                    the deplorable outrage at Cienfuegos and promises of vigorous action by the
                    Cuban Government toward the punishment of the perpetrators. This exhibition of
                    good will by the Cuban Government is highly appreciated by the Government of the
                    United States.)</p>
            </div>
